OVERVIEW = r"""# Neural Volatility Surface Forecasting Lab: Colab notebook

**Authoritative notebook.** (`notebooks/exploratory/Neural_Volatility_Surface_Colab.ipynb` is an older exploratory, contract-level demo and is kept unchanged.) This file is generated by `scripts/build_colab_notebook.py` from the unit-tested package `backend/src/volatility_lab`; every module is embedded below, so a fresh runtime needs nothing but this notebook.

**Research objective.** Build implied-volatility (IV) surfaces from hosted option-chain data, forecast how the surface changes, and judge neural models *honestly* against simple baselines. It is a research and education tool, not a trading system, and it makes no profitability claim.

**Methodology.** hosted chain -> reject-ledgered validation -> parity forward / discount factor -> OTM mid prices -> Black-76 IV -> constant-maturity grid (tenor x log-moneyness) with *observed / interpolated / missing* cell status and no extrapolation -> leakage-safe features -> baselines (persistence, rolling mean, ridge, PCA-ridge) -> GPU-only neural models (MLP, GRU) -> expanding-window walk-forward evaluation -> reports and hashed artifacts.

**Dataset.** `dudesurfin/spy-options-eod-volatility-surface-2010-2023` on Kaggle (SPY end-of-day option chains; uploader-stated MIT licence; upstream source OptionsDX). Accessed with the official Kaggle client directly from this runtime; no copy is made to your computer, Drive or Git. **Upstream terms are not verified**: see the data notes in Section 5 and `docs/data/HOSTED_DATASET_ASSESSMENT.md`.

**Target.** `y(t+h, cell) - s(t, cell)`: the change in IV of each (tenor, moneyness) cell over `h` trading days (default `h = 1`), evaluated on cells that are **observed** at the target date and have a real value at the forecast origin.

**Models.** persistence, rolling mean, ridge, PCA-ridge, MLP, GRU (3 seeds each plus a seed-average). A Transformer is deliberately not included: roughly 3,000 daily samples do not justify it.

**Evaluation.** Chronological expanding-window folds (validation = the year before each test year; no test-year tuning); descriptive MAE/RMSE in vol points with sample counts, by tenor, moneyness, year and realised-vol regime. **No statistical-significance claim is made** (the Phase 0 inference audit closed NO-GO, so inferential validity is unsupported).

**Known limitations.** SPY options are American-style while Black-76 is European (OTM quotes only mitigate this); closing-snapshot mids, not executable prices; forward and discount factor inferred from put-call parity; one underlying, one vendor; the dataset's upstream licence is unverified; backtest only, not live.
"""

